WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.810
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.301
being released all the time,

00:00:06.301 --> 00:00:07.926
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:07.926 --> 00:00:09.428
to test for ourselves.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.933
We're starting off strong with

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:14.741
the KVD Beauty Good Apple

00:00:14.741 --> 00:00:17.200
Skin-Perfecting Foundation Balm.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.014
This is the first KVD product

00:00:19.014 --> 00:00:21.028
I've seen hyped in about five years

00:00:21.028 --> 00:00:23.678
and the first one I've
tried since the rebrand.

00:00:23.678 --> 00:00:26.558
This foundation looks
incredible on the skin.

00:00:26.558 --> 00:00:28.998
Like, my skin really did look perfected

00:00:28.998 --> 00:00:31.280
and healthy, and it's
definitely buildable,

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.010
so you can get whatever
coverage you want from it.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.370
However, as an oily person,

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.900
I gotta say this was not meant for us.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.690
Which, like, with "balm" in the name,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.600
you probably didn't need
me to tell you that.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.670
Here's what I looked like
at the end of the day.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.589
I looked like a greasy little piggy.

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:49.410
Dry-skinned people, you need this.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.680
Next up we got the Kiss Eyebrow Top Coat,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.210
which is exactly what it says.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.680
It's a long-wearing
topcoat for your brows.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.346
It felt really weird to paint this

00:00:57.346 --> 00:00:58.860
on my brows, but I did it.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.901
And it actually is smudge-proof,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:01.840
for the most part.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.090
Like, I was rubbing hard,

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.448
and I saw barely any transfer.

00:01:05.448 --> 00:01:07.500
The waterproof claim was also true.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.550
Here's what they looked
like before I showered,

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.550
and here's what they looked like after.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.380
Literally no change.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.655
And of course I had to see

00:01:14.655 --> 00:01:16.513
if the 24-hour claim was true,

00:01:16.513 --> 00:01:18.490
so I went to bed wearing the brow topcoat.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.698
And even though they didn't look

00:01:19.698 --> 00:01:22.013
100% perfect the next day,

00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:23.796
I do think this made my brow product

00:01:23.796 --> 00:01:26.249
last so much longer.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.860
[sighs] Oh, boy, here we go.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.542
The Colourpop Cheek Dew Serum Blush.

00:01:30.542 --> 00:01:32.760
I am devastated that this was not

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.580
as good as I wanted it to be.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.020
So, I applied foundation to
the right side of my face

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.703
and left the left side bare,

00:01:38.703 --> 00:01:40.428
just in case it performed better

00:01:40.428 --> 00:01:42.540
on one side rather than the other.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.031
And I do think it performs

00:01:44.031 --> 00:01:46.350
slightly better on bare skin.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.208
It's just a very oily texture

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.575
that didn't seem to blend well

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.137
on top of foundation.

00:01:51.137 --> 00:01:53.243
And since the color is so sheer,

00:01:53.243 --> 00:01:54.559
I had to apply more,

00:01:54.559 --> 00:01:56.592
which made my foundation move around,

00:01:56.592 --> 00:01:58.441
and it was just a mess.

00:01:58.441 --> 00:02:00.920
If you want a better alternative
to something like this,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.511
I'd go for the Em Cosmetics

00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:04.419
Color Drops Serum Blush.

00:02:04.419 --> 00:02:07.410
I am not a body-foundation kind of person,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.800
so I was nervous to try the

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.464
Fenty Beauty Body Sauce
Body Luminizing Tint.

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:14.480
It's basically like a shimmery body tint,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.110
so it adds a bit of color.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.101
I definitely needed a lighter shade,

00:02:18.101 --> 00:02:20.397
but this product actually
performed way better

00:02:20.397 --> 00:02:23.010
and less messy than I thought it would.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.309
I preferred applying it with my

00:02:24.309 --> 00:02:25.842
Fenty face and body brush,

00:02:25.842 --> 00:02:27.270
but hands are fine too.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.836
I thought the glow it gave my skin

00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:30.811
was really pretty, and
it didn't feel sticky,

00:02:30.811 --> 00:02:32.100
which I know a lot of people

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.143
hated about the Fenty Body Lava,

00:02:34.143 --> 00:02:36.170
which is a similar body product.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.765
It did dry down and felt
lightweight on the skin,

00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:40.580
and it said it was transfer-resistant,

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.582
so I tried wiping it with a paper towel,

00:02:42.582 --> 00:02:43.798
and there was some transfer

00:02:43.798 --> 00:02:45.498
but nothing too terrible.

00:02:47.692 --> 00:02:50.150
I was very intrigued to
try this brow pencil.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.383
This is the Huda Beauty

00:02:51.383 --> 00:02:53.791
#BombBrows Microshade Brow Pencil,

00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:57.350
which supposedly has the
thinnest tip on the market.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.190
Here's how thin a brow stroke is

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:01.820
with this pencil compared
to my regular one.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.870
I really liked this.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.610
I kind of like how the body of the pencil

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.550
has this, like, diamond shape.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.572
I felt like it was very easy to hold

00:03:10.572 --> 00:03:11.884
and maneuver in my hand,

00:03:11.884 --> 00:03:14.400
and it also feels more
expensive than it is.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.450
It's one of the cheaper
high-end brow pencils,

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.152
at just $17.

00:03:18.152 --> 00:03:19.227
But here's the thing:

00:03:19.227 --> 00:03:22.244
I think for the amount of
pressure I normally apply,

00:03:22.244 --> 00:03:26.000
the thin microfine point
is just super fragile.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.900
Like, I broke it more than once.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.220
So maybe there's a reason that

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.570
there aren't more brow pencils

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:31.990
with these extra-thin tips,

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.265
but I do like how this made my brows look.

